<title>BELGIUM: EU panel to discuss duty-free Canada wheat imports.</title>
<headline>EU panel to discuss duty-free Canada wheat imports.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-02-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>European Union grain officials will on Thursday discuss arrangements for importing 300,000 tonnes of Canadian quality wheat duty free in 1997, EU and Canadian officials said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>They will discuss the split between durum and soft wheat, number and timing of quota tranches.</p>
<p>Canada is looking for more transparent and predictable management of the duty free import quota, which was agreed under a 1992 GATT oilseeds panel ruling to compensate Canadian exporters for trade losses due to EU production subsidies.</p>
<p>EU grain officials, gathering for the weekly meeting of the EU cereals management committee, are also due to discuss national cereals food aid programmes.</p>
</text>
